# device_lifecycle_resume_registers: 0x1024 and 0x1028. A root resume with a child still faulted raises the interrupt again and 0x102c stays 1; the child's resume clears it. Resuming a FIFO that is not faulted, with no FIFO at all, a child id that is not defined, 63, and 64 (past the child slots, resuming nothing, and whose 1 << 64 shifts as 1 << 0 on arm64: it clears the root's fault bit without resuming it); ten resumes of a healthy child report a stamp-wait timeout each, later ones only log. Wakes (0x1020) of 0, 64, 0xffffffff and a child that does not exist do nothing.
